<title>FRANCE: French sugar consumption rose in July - FIRS.</title>
<headline>French sugar consumption rose in July - FIRS.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>French sugar consumption rose to a provisional 200,000 tonnes in July 1996 from 188,000 tonnes in June 1996 and 170,488 in July 1995, the FIRS sugar intervention board said on Friday.</p>
<p>This brought cumulative sales to the French market in the first 10 months of the 1995/96 (Oct/Sept) season to 1.65 million tonnes compared with 1.63 million a year earlier, FIRS said in its September report.</p>
<p>--Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
